      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.082,
          "end": 3.45,
          "en": "(gentle music)",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.45,
          "end": 6.12,
          "en": "-: So in the previous video when we talked about the fetch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.12,
          "end": 9,
          "en": "eager, and lazy, in between, we talked about caching.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9,
          "end": 11.91,
          "en": "And then I thought, \"Okay, we need to discuss this more.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.91,
          "end": 13.38,
          "en": "So basically what happens is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.38,
          "end": 16.74,
          "en": "so let's say we got a React client and then we got a server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.74,
          "end": 17.82,
          "en": "and then we got database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.82,
          "end": 19.74,
          "en": "So let's say we got this three layers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 19.74,
          "end": 22.41,
          "en": "Every time a user sends a request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.41,
          "end": 25.14,
          "en": "let's say for saving data or fetching data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.14,
          "end": 26.88,
          "en": "basically that request goes to the server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 26.88,
          "end": 27.713,
          "en": "and server says,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 27.713,
          "end": 30.15,
          "en": "\"Okay, we have to do something with the database.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 30.15,
          "end": 32.55,
          "en": "So it will open the session for the database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 32.55,
          "end": 33.99,
          "en": "and then it'll fetch the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 33.99,
          "end": 35.76,
          "en": "So let's say for a particular query,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 35.76,
          "end": 39.21,
          "en": "you want to fetch the data about alien with 101,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 39.21,
          "end": 40.65,
          "en": "the request goes to the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 40.65,
          "end": 42.87,
          "en": "Server says, \"Okay, I don't have this data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 42.87,
          "end": 45.27,
          "en": "and I'm in session S1,\" let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 45.27,
          "end": 47.437,
          "en": "And then the request goes to the database by saying,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 47.437,
          "end": 49.11,
          "en": "\"Okay, I want this data.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 49.11,
          "end": 51,
          "en": "Now session one got data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 51,
          "end": 54.15,
          "en": "and then it'll return to the user, and everything is happy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 54.15,
          "end": 55.29,
          "en": "So let's say in the same session,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 55.29,
          "end": 57.87,
          "en": "you're fetching for 101 alien and then 102 alien.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 57.87,
          "end": 59.58,
          "en": "Of course, it will fire two queries",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 59.58,
          "end": 61.68,
          "en": "because there are two different data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 61.68,
          "end": 66.68,
          "en": "But what if you fire for 101 two times in the same session?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 66.96,
          "end": 67.98,
          "en": "Now in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 67.98,
          "end": 70.28999999999999,
          "en": "it will file the query to the database for the first time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 70.28999999999999,
          "end": 72.21000000000001,
          "en": "and say, \"Okay, I got this data.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 72.21000000000001,
          "end": 74.43,
          "en": "And now when you are sending the request for the second time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 74.43,
          "end": 76.74,
          "en": "with the same session, in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 76.74,
          "end": 78.93,
          "en": "don't you think for the 101 you already have a data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 78.93,
          "end": 79.763,
          "en": "in this session?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 79.763,
          "end": 81.81,
          "en": "And your hibernate says, \"Yeah, that's smart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 81.81,
          "end": 82.77,
          "en": "Now we can use it.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 82.77,
          "end": 84.9,
          "en": "It will not file this database query for the second request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 84.9,
          "end": 86.97,
          "en": "It will say, \"Okay, same session, same data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 86.97,
          "end": 89.67,
          "en": "I will return that this to the user.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 89.67,
          "end": 91.47,
          "en": "So that's how caching works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 91.47,
          "end": 92.303,
          "en": "Now is it a good thing?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 92.303,
          "end": 95.58,
          "en": "Of course, you are saving some requests with the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 95.58,
          "end": 97.53,
          "en": "Is it the bad thing? Sometime.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 97.53,
          "end": 100.41,
          "en": "What if you have the data changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 100.41,
          "end": 102.06,
          "en": "while you are sending this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 102.06,
          "end": 105.09,
          "en": "So let's say you got the first request, you have fetched it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 105.09,
          "end": 107.16,
          "en": "For the second request in the same session,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 107.16,
          "end": 109.92,
          "en": "meanwhile, you're not fetching it, what if there...",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 109.92,
          "end": 112.97999999999999,
          "en": "Because of some different activity, the data got changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 112.97999999999999,
          "end": 113.813,
          "en": "Okay, so that's something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 113.813,
          "end": 115.77000000000001,
          "en": "you have to also keep into your mind,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 115.77000000000001,
          "end": 117.75,
          "en": "when to use cache, when not to use cache.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 117.75,
          "end": 120,
          "en": "So by default hibernate will provide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 120,
          "end": 121.29,
          "en": "this particular caching technique",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 121.29,
          "end": 123.45,
          "en": "and this is called L1 cache.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 123.45,
          "end": 127.35,
          "en": "But what if you got session one, let's say S1,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 127.35,
          "end": 130.32,
          "en": "and in this session, you got the alien data 101",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 130.32,
          "end": 131.79,
          "en": "and you have it there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 131.79,
          "end": 134.67,
          "en": "And now you got a new session",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 134.67,
          "end": 137.85,
          "en": "in which the user is asking for the same data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 137.85,
          "end": 140.49,
          "en": "Can this two session, S1 and S2, interact?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 140.49,
          "end": 141.57,
          "en": "And the answer is no.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 141.57,
          "end": 143.85,
          "en": "By default, hibernate will not allow it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 143.85,
          "end": 145.74,
          "en": "In case if you want to achieve that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 145.74,
          "end": 148.41,
          "en": "we have to use some external application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 148.41,
          "end": 151.56,
          "en": "who will provide the level 2 caching, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 151.56,
          "end": 154.77,
          "en": "So hibernate do uses JCache to achieve this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 154.77,
          "end": 157.11,
          "en": "And Jcache being a standard,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 157.11,
          "end": 158.37,
          "en": "there are multiple implementation for this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 158.37,
          "end": 159.84,
          "en": "We got Ehcache, caffeine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 159.84,
          "end": 162.69,
          "en": "There's a bunch of libraries available and you can use them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 162.69,
          "end": 166.23,
          "en": "But again, caching is good, but not always.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 166.23,
          "end": 169.11,
          "en": "So yeah, that's what I wanna talk about caching more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 169.11,
          "end": 170.31,
          "en": "from the previous video.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
